{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","max_tokens":768,"stream":true,"system":"Keep the answer short.","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Find the unique integer selector from 1 through 99 that has remainder 2 when divided by 5, remainder 0 when divided by 7, and remainder 7 when divided by 11. Work out the constraints before answering. Use get_value with the derived selector to obtain the stored value. Do not guess the stored value."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need x satisfying all three congruences between 1 and 99, so I'm checking multiples of 7 against the mod 5 and mod 11 conditions, narrowing candidates to 7, 42, and 77 so far based on the mod 5 check, and now verifying 42 against mod 11.\n\n42 mod 11 is 9, and 77 mod 11 is 0, so neither works, but 7 satisfies all three: mod 5 gives 2, mod 7 gives 0, mod 11 gives 7. Since the modulus 385 exceeds the range 1-99, this solution is unique, so x = 7. Now I'll call get_value(7).\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018N79V8eNHc59JBbQKssgTu","name":"get_value","input":{"selector":7},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_018N79V8eNHc59JBbQKssgTu","content":"7"}]}],"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"tools":[{"name":"get_value","description":"Return the stored integer for the selector.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"selector":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["selector"],"additionalProperties":false}}],"tool_choice":{"type":"auto"},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}}